---
const tapeName = "tape://20.2.272.tape";
const mirrorRoot = "https://20-2-272.tapekit.org/";
const versionedPrefix = "https://20-2-272.tapekit.org/civicord/uk-2024-25/holborn-and-st-pancras/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11";
const versionedIndex = `${versionedPrefix}/index.html`;
const verifyPage = `${versionedPrefix}/verify.html`;
const manifestUrl = `${versionedPrefix}/manifest.json`;
const publicGuide = "https://github.com/sneldao/civicord/blob/main/docs/deweb-mirror.md";
const manifestSha256 = "2993bbce8d018be26a1664abcb586f5b034cbb6fd7732c4a17e056e877465901";
const container = "0xB078da6de46795656187052322Dda3A7E249C288";
const pinnedBlock = "76865195";
const directCommand = "python3 scripts/tapeout/verify_deweb.py data/out/deweb/holborn-and-st-pancras/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11 --container 0xB078da6de46795656187052322Dda3A7E249C288 --prefix civicord/uk-2024-25/holborn-and-st-pancras/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11";
---

<section class="tapeout-mirror" aria-labelledby="tapeout-mirror-title">
  <p class="tapeout-kicker">Experimental publication mirror</p>
  <h2 id="tapeout-mirror-title">Check this seat's evidence bundle independently</h2>
  <p>
    The seven-candidate Holborn and St Pancras cohort was exported as a versioned evidence bundle and
    mirrored to X Layer DeWEB. This page remains the canonical Civicord reading interface. The mirror is
    a static copy for continuity and hash checking — not a second source of truth and not a current
    availability check.
  </p>

  <div class="record-actions tapeout-actions" aria-label="Open the mirror and verification material">
    <a class="btn-primary" href={mirrorRoot} rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the mirror</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={versionedIndex} rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the fixed version</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={verifyPage} rel="noopener noreferrer">Bundle verification page</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={publicGuide} rel="noopener noreferrer">Public verification guide</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={manifestUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">manifest.json</a>
    <button type="button" class="btn-ghost" data-copy-text={manifestSha256} data-copy-done="Manifest hash copied.">Copy manifest hash</button>
    <span class="pair-copy-status" role="status"></span>
  </div>

  <dl class="tapeout-facts">
    <div>
      <dt>Bundle version</dt>
      <dd><code>audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11</code></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Manifest SHA-256</dt>
      <dd><code>{manifestSha256}</code></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Tape name</dt>
      <dd><code>{tapeName}</code></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Container</dt>
      <dd><code>{container}</code></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Verification</dt>
      <dd>7 files matched at pinned block <code>{pinnedBlock}</code></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Contents</dt>
      <dd>methodology, caveats, sources, records and hashes</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <details class="tapeout-direct">
    <summary>Direct-chain verification details</summary>
    <p>
      The independent check did not use the gateway response. It read the file bytes from X Layer at one
      pinned block through two RPC endpoints, checked the pinned SiteRegistry implementation and compared
      size plus SHA-256 for all seven frozen files. The command was run from the repository root:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{directCommand}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Report: <code>data/out/deweb/verification/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11-b078da6de4.json</code>.
      X Layer's public RPC-operator set is thin, so this is evidence of consistent chain-state reads, not
      a claim of perfect censorship resistance or permanence.
    </p>
  </details>

  <p class="muted tapeout-limits">
    Important limits: the container holder can technically write paths in the container. Civicord's policy is an
    append-only versioned publication policy, so citations should use the fixed versioned URL and its manifest hash.
    Responses such as DNS errors, redirects and HTTP 403 are technical classes, not allegations of intent.
    The mirror omits bulk claim diffs because their scope caveats need review.
  </p>
</section>
